Taking $ABC$ to be the base of pyramid $ABCH$, the height is $HD$.  Therefore, the volume of pyramid $ABCH$ is $$\frac{[ABC](HD)}{3}.$$We are given that this volume equals 20, so we have \[{[ABC]\cdot HD}=60.\]The volume of prism $ABCDEFGH$ is the product of area of $ABCD$ and the height of the prism, which equals $HD$.   The area of $ABC$ is half the area of rectangle $ABCD$, so we have  \begin{align*}
\text{Volume of }ABCDEFGH &= ([ABCD])(HD) \\
&= 2([ABC])(HD) \\
&= \boxed{120}.\end{align*}

problem:
Let \[f(n) =
\begin{cases}
4n+3 &\text{if }n<a, \\
7n-12 &\text{if }n\ge{a}.
\end{cases}
\]Find $a$ if the graph of $y=f(n)$ is continuous.

reference_solution:
A $y$-intercept is a point on the graph that lies on the $y$-axis, so $x = 0$.  Hence, the number $y$-intercepts corresponds to the number of real solutions of the quadratic equation $y^2 - 4y - 1 = 0$.  The discriminant of this quadratic equation is $(-4)^2 + 4 \cdot 1 \cdot (-1) = 20$, which is positive, so the quadratic has two distinct real roots.  Therefore, the number of $y$-intercepts is $\boxed{2}$.

